The construction I’m implementing stays in the paper’s plane-graph objects. It uses a chain of symmetric pentagonal faces: each face has two indistinguishable radial completion choices, while exact diameter sentinels couple neighboring choices. Sampling one global phase first gives a certificate without solving; the complementary phase is the only other solution. The verifier checks face membership and recomputes graph diameter by BFS.
